Shortest Path
-------------
https://github.com/Skretzo/shortest-path by Skretzo and contributors

The walking map used for the guide line (src/main/resources/com/herbrunhelper/walk-map.zip) is
Shortest Path's collision map (src/main/resources/collision-map.zip, from commit a7dd4a2), included
unchanged. The doors, gates, stairs, ladders and shortcuts the line can use
(src/main/resources/com/herbrunhelper/walk-links.tsv) and what they need
(src/main/resources/com/herbrunhelper/walk-reqs.tsv: skill levels, quests, items, varbits and
varplayers) are taken from its transport lists (transports/transports.tsv and
transports/agility_shortcuts.tsv), with item group names turned into item ids from its
item-variations.tsv, by scripts/build_walk_links.py. WalkRequirements.java checks them the way
Shortest Path defines them; that code is written anew, not copied. When both plugins
are installed and the setting is on, Farm Run Optimizer can also send Shortest Path the next stop
(through RuneLite's plugin messages) so it draws its own line.

The guide line's end-point rule (nearest reachable tile around the target, sides before corners)
and the fairy ring travel log highlight follow how Shortest Path does them (ReachableGoalRule and
PathAnnotator); they were written anew here, not copied. RouteSession.java ports the rules
Shortest Path's scheduler uses to decide when to work a route out again (PathScheduler.isNearPath
and RefreshCoordinator.offRouteTick, with its default recalculate distance of 10 tiles), and
PathGuide's end-point tiers and wallSeparated check follow ReachableGoalRule and
TargetGoals.wallSeparated, under the license below.

